---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Data attribution — The Sustainability Diet" description="Attribution for the third-party scientific data sources used by the Near Time atlas: PBDB, Neotoma, USDA PLANTS, GBIF, iNaturalist.">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-reading px-6 pt-20 pb-32">

    <p class="small-caps text-xs text-ochre mb-4">Data attribution</p>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-5xl tracking-tight leading-tight mb-4">
      Data attribution.
    </h1>
    <p class="font-serif text-lg md:text-xl leading-relaxed text-ink/75 mb-12 max-w-reading">
      The Near Time atlas is built on open scientific datasets.
      Each source is acknowledged below, at the component level
      inside each vignette, and at the page level in the
      <a href="/near-time/sources" class="text-ochre hover:underline">sources &amp; methodology</a>
      page. The licenses below govern reuse.
    </p>

    <div class="prose-reading text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/85 space-y-10">

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          Paleobiology Database (PBDB).
        </h2>
        <p>
          Source: <a href="https://paleobiodb.org" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">paleobiodb.org</a>.
          License: CC-BY.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/75">
          Attribution: &ldquo;Fossil occurrence data from the
          Paleobiology Database (paleobiodb.org), licensed CC-BY.&rdquo;
          The PBDB is the primary source for all Late Pleistocene
          vertebrate occurrence data displayed on this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          Neotoma Paleoecology Database.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Source: <a href="https://www.neotomadb.org" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">neotomadb.org</a>.
          License: CC-BY-4.0.
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/75">
          Attribution: &ldquo;Paleoecological data from the Neotoma
          Paleoecology Database (neotomadb.org), licensed CC-BY-4.0.&rdquo;
          Neotoma provides the pollen, plant-macrofossil, and
          vertebrate-occurrence records used for plant-community
          reconstructions.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          USDA PLANTS.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Source: <a href="https://plants.usda.gov" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">plants.usda.gov</a>.
          License: public domain (United States Government work).
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/75">
          Used for modern plant distribution, taxonomy, and
          species-code normalization. Attribution is courtesy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          GBIF.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Source: <a href="https://www.gbif.org" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">gbif.org</a>.
          License: varies by dataset; records used here are filtered
          to CC0, CC-BY, or CC-BY-NC (where compatible with this
          site's non-commercial editorial use).
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/75">
          Attribution for GBIF-sourced records follows the GBIF
          citation convention: Dataset DOI(s) are listed in each
          component that uses them, along with the date of access.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          iNaturalist.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Source: <a href="https://www.inaturalist.org" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">inaturalist.org</a>.
          License: varies per observation; observations used here
          are filtered to research-grade and to observer-selected
          CC licenses (CC0, CC-BY, CC-BY-NC).
        </p>
        <p class="text-ink/75">
          Per-observation attribution to the observer is carried in
          the component that uses each record.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          Base maps.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Natural Earth (<a href="https://www.naturalearthdata.com" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">naturalearthdata.com</a>),
          public domain; used for continental and regional base
          maps. OpenStreetMap contributors (<a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org" class="text-ochre hover:underline" rel="noopener">openstreetmap.org</a>),
          ODbL; used where OpenStreetMap is specifically attributed
          in a component.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          Fonts.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Fraunces by Phaedra Charles and Flavia Zimbardi (SIL OFL).
          Inter by Rasmus Andersson (SIL OFL). Source Serif 4 by
          Frank Grie&szlig;hammer (SIL OFL). All used under the
          SIL Open Font License.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-tight mb-4">
          Report an error.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Attribution errors, missing credits, or license concerns:
          <a href="mailto:karen@paleofoundation.com" class="text-ochre hover:underline">karen@paleofoundation.com</a>.
          These are corrected as fast as they can be verified.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
